<title>UK: Legal &amp; General sets new peak on bid talk.</title>
<headline>Legal &amp; General sets new peak on bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Legal &amp; General rose to a fresh record peak amid renewed takeover speculation, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0850 GMT, the shares were up 10p to 795p, after stretching as high as 799p.  </p>
<p>The UK insurer has been the subject of takeover talk since last week when Lloyds TSB said it would buy the rest of Lloyds Abbey Life which it did not already own.</p>
<p>&quot;Legal &amp; General has been a focus (of takeover speculation) ever since the Lloyds news,&quot; said one trader. &quot;It may be a case of two plus two equals five, but that's the talk.&quot;</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
